WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.500
Coding agents write code fast.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.800
Merging it safely is the hard part.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.400
Branches pile up.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.633
Tests get skipped.

00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:10.300
Agents collide on files.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.333
Yesterday's lessons are gone.

00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:15.800
rota is a workflow for Claude Code and Codex.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.833
You write work down as issues.

00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:21.167
Agents build each one in small, verified commits.

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:24.933
One small binary sets up a project in one command.

00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:28.267
Backlog, knowledge and decisions live in the repo.

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:31.200
Every branch is reviewed against its spec.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.000
Only work that passes your tests lands on main.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.400
Lessons and decisions stay in the repo, so the next session starts ahead.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.867
rota makes sure what they merge works.

